{"file_path": "/home/digimonk/.claude/projects/-home-digimonk-Projects-SU2ZX-Foundation-Code-Package-SU2ZX/memory/function-inventory-self-inventory-constraint.md", "content": "---\nname: function-inventory-self-inventory-constraint\ndescription: Why tools/function_inventory.py must keep main() at line 10 with its legacy write and zero parameters, and what review must not prescribe\nmetadata:\n  pinned: false\n---\n\n`tools/function_inventory.py` scans the `tools/` directory, so it inventories **itself**. The\ngenerated `docs/CODE_FUNCTION_INVENTORY.md` records, for `main`, its `node.lineno`, its unparsed\nargument list, and the deduplicated set of direct call expressions inside its body. The committed\ninventory is therefore a fixed point: any edit that moves `main` off line 10, adds or removes a\nparameter, or drops the `project_path(\"docs/CODE_FUNCTION_INVENTORY.md\").write_text(...)` call\nchanges the tool's own inventory section and breaks byte-identity against the committed artifact.\n\nThe user has stated directly that this structure is mandated and that review must **not** prescribe\nremoving the legacy write from `main()` or converting the module globals (`ROOT`, `DIRECTORIES`,\n`TEST_DIRECTORIES`, `OUTPUT`) into explicit `main()` parameters. The deliberate idiom is to keep the\nconfiguration block *below* `main` and to override the globals from the `__main__` argparse block.\nWhen reviewing or refactoring this file, treat the \"globals below main, called with no arguments\"\npattern as a hard constraint and direct any purity or testability concerns elsewhere (for example,\nat the CLI entry block), not at `main`'s signature or its legacy write.\n\nRelatedly, `src/su2zx/paths.py::project_path` already resolves its argument, handles absolute inputs\nexplicitly, and raises if the result escapes the current working directory, so review should not ask\nfor an extra resolve-and-compare wrapper around paths that already pass through it.\n"}
::/write::
